"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[52298],{452298:e=>{e.exports="# Setup Pipeline\n\nThis skill guides you through setting up a newly created pipeline with initial datasets. Use this workflow after the pipeline creation agent hands over a blank pipeline.\n\n## Workflow Overview\n\nFollow this sequence when setting up a new pipeline:\n\n**IMPORTANT: DO NOT call `readPipelineDetails` or `listFiles`**\n\n```\n1. Gather Data Context\n   └── Use readTable/getSqlSample to understand source data\n       ├── Identify schema, columns, data types\n       └── Understand data relationships\n\n2. Present the user with two options:\n   └── They can propose a pipeline architecture of their choice\n   └── You can propose an architecture, which they can iteratively modify\n       └── If they use your template, ask for confirmation or modifications\n\n3. Create Pipeline Files (parallel)\n   └── Use createPipelineFile for all dataset files in parallel\n\n4. Write File Content\n   └── Use workspaceUpdateFile to write transformation code for all files\n   └── Ensure all dependencies are implemented correctly\n   └── Use Python by default\n```\n\n## Key Principles\n\n### Parallel Operations\n\n**IMPORTANT: When working with multiple files, You MUST use parallel tool calls for efficiency:**\n\n- **ALWAYS call `createPipelineFile` for multiple files in parallel** (use a single message with multiple tool calls)\n- **DO NOT wait for individual file operations to complete before starting the next** - batch them together\n"}}]);
